{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"active-ambigious-steer","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Unified demand-side cost-reduction program for rebar's LLM operations, the first line of defense in the layered spend-governance model (ahead of warning alarms and the hard cap). Goal: reduce steady-state token spend and peak-day spend while holding review quality, measured against existing per-review and per-ticket unit-cost baselines and the unit-economics dashboards. Children cover: batched code-review criteria passes, re-review cycle caps with explicit override, lower-cost model evaluation for Sonnet-tier operations, and lite review tiers for low-complexity work. Acceptance: each child lands with before/after unit-cost measurements; combined effect visible in the unit-economics metrics.","id":"887c-009e-bc96-48c8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["cost","governance"],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Reduce LLM gate unit costs (demand-side cost program)"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1789406124341874001,"uuid":"adf65132-2eb0-4896-8d33-aa2b78ba219f"}